---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'; import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro'; import CallToAction from '../components/CallToAction.astro'; import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Install and Start FM AI Assistent" description="Install FM AI Assistent on Windows 11 or Linux, load your Football Manager 2026 save and configure an optional AI provider." path="/getting-started/">
  <div class="page-shell"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Getting started'}]} /><header class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">First session</p><h1>Install and start FM AI Assistent.</h1><p class="lead">Download an official package, load a Football Manager 2026 career and create the first local data snapshot before connecting optional AI features.</p></header>
    <section class="section content-grid"><article class="prose"><h2>1. Download the application</h2><p>Open the <a href={site.latestRelease} rel="noopener noreferrer">latest GitHub release</a>. The packaged desktop application is recommended; a native image and Java 25+ JAR are also documented. Choose an asset for Windows or Linux as identified by that release.</p><h2>2. Start both applications</h2><ol><li>Start Football Manager 2026 and fully load a save.</li><li>Launch FM AI Assistent as the same computer user.</li><li>If a browser does not open, visit <code>http://127.0.0.1:8080</code>.</li><li>If 8080 is already occupied, check the startup log for 8081, 8082 or the next selected port.</li></ol><h2>3. Load your save data</h2><p>Select <strong>Load data</strong>. Wait for the player, staff, club and competition phases to complete. You can now browse those tabs without configuring an AI provider.</p><h2>4. Add an assistant (optional)</h2><h3>Codex</h3><p>Install Codex CLI, select Codex in the AI assistant and complete the ChatGPT sign-in. If the FM tools are unavailable, add the local MCP endpoint:</p><pre class="code-block"><code>codex mcp add fm-ai-assistent \
  --url http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp</code></pre><h3>GitHub Copilot</h3><p>Install Copilot CLI, use the embedded GitHub sign-in, and add the local endpoint when it is not already listed:</p><pre class="code-block"><code>copilot mcp add --transport http \
  fm-ai-assistent http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp</code></pre><h3>Antigravity</h3><p>Install and sign in to Antigravity, configure <code>fm-ai-assistent</code> at the local MCP URL and merge the documented FM26 tool permissions into your existing settings. The repository README has the current complete permission list.</p><h3>OpenRouter</h3><p>Select OpenRouter, submit the masked API key and choose a route or model. Free capacity and limits are not guaranteed. Paid models and the Auto router may incur charges and require confirmation.</p><h2>5. Control context</h2><p>Open <strong>Context</strong> to enable or disable managed-club and tactic information. Add an exported <code>.fmf</code> tactic if your question depends on roles or instructions.</p><h2>6. Refresh when needed</h2><p>Select <strong>Load data</strong> again after opening another save, changing clubs or advancing to information you need updated.</p><h2>Troubleshooting</h2><h3>No FM26 data is found</h3><ul><li>Confirm FM26 is running and the save is fully loaded.</li><li>Run both applications as the same computer user and, on Windows, at the same administrator level.</li><li>Select <strong>Load data</strong> again.</li></ul><h3>An agent is unavailable</h3><p>Install its CLI, finish the normal account login and restart FM AI Assistent so it can detect the command.</p><h3>The app does not open</h3><p>Open the loopback URL manually. Desktop logs are stored at <code>~/.fm-ai-assistent/fm-ai-assistent.log</code>.</p></article><aside><div class="info-card"><h3>Security baseline</h3><p>Keep the application bound to its default loopback address. Review every agent permission and do not publish API keys, logs or local MCP endpoints to the internet.</p></div><div class="info-card" style="margin-top:1rem"><h3>Need the exact current setup?</h3><p>Provider CLIs evolve. The repository README is the source of truth for the application’s current integration commands.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${site.repository}#use-the-ai-assistant`} rel="noopener noreferrer">Read provider setup →</a></div></aside></section>
  </div><CallToAction eyebrow="All set" title="Load the save. Ask the football question." />
</BaseLayout>
